  "ops.seqTitle": "Same stops, different order: pure priority order = most urgent stop first regardless of the way; nearest neighbour = always to the closest stop. “Priority” = extra km compared with the shortest run and the priority-weighted mean distance to the stops (this run instead of the shortest run).",
  "ops.osrmUnreachable": "OSRM not reachable: km by straight line × 1.35, next attempt in 2 min at the earliest",
  "ops.orderPerRunPrio": "<b>Order per run:</b> objective = distance + λ × priority-weighted mean distance to the stops (Σ wᵢ·dᵢ ÷ Σ wᵢ; dᵢ = km from the depot to stop i, wᵢ = priority − lowest priority of the run). λ comes from the “priority ↔ distance” slider ({levels}): λ = 1 means reaching the urgent stops 1 km earlier is worth a 1 km detour; λ = 0 is pure kilometre optimisation, as are equal priorities. Up to {exactMax} stops per group exact (Held-Karp), above that nearest neighbour (plain and with priority), pure priority order and further start points, each improved with 2-opt and Or-opt on the full objective. Rebalancing and station balancing: first all pickups, then all drop-offs, both optimised together. Kilometres with “road routing” (default): road matrix of the OSRM demo server (without traffic; up to {osrmMax} points per request, cached, at most one request per second), driving time from the driven route; without road routing or on failure straight line × {detour} at {speedKmh} km/h. The time limit applies to planning, by road a run may exceed it slightly (marked). On-site times: 1.5 min pick up, 1 min drop off, 2.5 min battery, 3 min workshop.",
  "ops.prioValues": "<b>Priority per stop</b> (0 = not urgent, 1 = urgent, up to 1.5 with surcharge): battery swap {energyW} × energy gap (1 − charge ÷ threshold or 1 − range ÷ threshold, the larger) + {idleW} × idle time (full from {idleRefH} h); pickup and workshop: idle time or time disabled (full from {idleRefH} h); from {longIdleH} h +{longIdleBonus} each. Drop-off: shortfall ÷ {needRef} (at most 1), spot without an available vehicle nearby or empty station +{emptyBonus}; pickup at a full station {fullStation}, otherwise 0. A stop with several vehicles counts with the most urgent one. The run card shows priority, rank and reason per stop, plus the km compared with pure priority order and nearest neighbour.",
  "ops.kmHOnDuty": "{km} km, {v1} h on duty, {v2}",
