  "ops.srcLimitRule": "range threshold per source = min(form value, {share} % of the 95th percentile) if that is below {maxP95} km",
  "ops.uncertaintyH": "Uncertainty and stability",
  "ops.uncertaintyText": "Starts and ends are counts (Poisson). <b>Balancing:</b> Σ starts and Σ ends of a municipality should be equal but are not: deployments and returns from the warehouse count as ends, trips across the municipal boundary and at the edge of the measurement window only on one side (31/10–01/11/2026 without gap bands: Stuttgart 11 %, Frankfurt 10 % more ends than starts). The ends of each municipality are therefore multiplied by k = Σ starts ÷ Σ ends. The sums include the suppressed events (cell × band below 3, per municipality only as a sum), which are not assigned to any cell. Afterwards net outflow across the whole municipality is 0 and shows where vehicles leave faster than on average. Starts stay unchanged; the surplus ends are assumed to be distributed like the other ends. <b>Standard error</b> = √(starts + k² × ends) ÷ measured hours, <b>range</b> = net ± {z} × standard error. The MCDA uses the cautious <b>lower bound</b> max(0, net − {z} × standard error); the need uses the estimate. <b>Stability:</b> in addition to the ±20 % weight sensitivity, the starts and ends of every cell are redrawn {draws} times (Poisson bootstrap with a fixed seed: same input, same result); each draw recomputes balancing, standardisation and ranking. “Stable” means: the spot stays among the top spots in all weight variants and in at least {minShare} % of the draws; below that it is “uncertain” with the share.",
  "ops.swapRangeRule": "<b>Range relative to the source:</b> some feeds report only small ranges (Lime via MobiData BW: at most ≈ 14 km); with “below {std} km” a third of their scale would count as empty. Per source with at least {minN} ranges the threshold is therefore min(form value, {share} % of the 95th percentile of the range) if the 95th percentile is below {maxP95} km; otherwise the form value. {share} % matches the charge-level threshold, {maxP95} km × {share} % = {std} km (continuous transition). The threshold is shown in the feed check and per vehicle in ops/&lt;state&gt;.json (reichweiteSchwelleKm). If the range is calculated from the battery level, only the battery level counts as before. If a source reports the same range for almost all vehicles (placeholders such as Donkey Bavaria 1 km or nextbike 0 km: over 95 % identical values or a p5–p95 spread below 0.1 km), its range does not count; without a usable battery level the energy is then unknown, not low.",
  "lib.rangeLimit": "small range (95th percentile {p95} km < {max} km): range threshold {limit} km ({share} % of it) instead of {std} km",
  "lib.rangeFlat": "constant range (placeholder): not used for energy and battery swaps",
